<title>RUSSIA: Russian NGTS 96 pre-tax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Russian NGTS 96 pre-tax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>NOVOSIBIRSK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian regional telecoms company Novosibirskaya Gorodskaya Telefonnaya Set (NGTS) said on Thursday that it boosted 1996 pre-tax profit on an accruals basis to 40.53 million roubles from 16.38 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Spokesman Alexander Morozov said the company's subscriber base increased by 16,064 clients to 300,000 clients.</p>
<p>NGTS shareholders include OAO Svyazinvest, with 50.66 percent, Salomon Brothers (21 percent), CS First Boston (14 percent) and OAO Brokerkreditservice (four percent).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($1 = 5,741 roubles)</p>
